mantle rm520
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rm_hjalte_sootby
title the garden account
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=laborer
traits temper=calm talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk buries_a_stone_in_a_garden_row_when_a_debt_is_settled
likes barley_soup digging old_maps frosty_mornings
dislikes crowds haggling
fears a_wage_lost_to_bad_counting a_shallow_root_in_hard_ground
hopes a_berth_under_a_dry_sky a_garden_with_every_marker_buried
topics land +0.5 prices +0.4 work +0.3
styles comfort=practical gossip=discreet refuse=firm tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# can tell the difference between a wage and a favour down to the last copper and plants little stones for debts made good.

words
oath! = Lime in my soup | Stones among the seed
saying! = Bury the debt after the paying | Dig far enough for a root to hold
duechip = a bit of red brick | my marker above ground
paidchip = a buried white pebble | my quittance stone
rowend = the last thumb of soil | the bare strip at the row foot
soupgrain = the barley heart | a pale grain with a seam
handspade = my short digging iron | my narrow garden blade
plankload = the low timber pile | a yardful of boards
frostskin = a white scratch on the soil | frost at the rim
wrongroad = a mistaken pencil turn | a lane ending in ink
seaheap = a dry berth | my far-off bunk
coinbed = my little hiding place | the shallow stone pocket

any
opinion dole for 2 : If there's soup to spare it ought to reach a bowl before anybody counts what the hungry wolf owes.
opinion houses against 2 : A mark on a plank gets more respect than the sore back that fetched it. I've had cause to notice that.
opinion merchants against 2 : One price for the timber and another for waiting for it. The timber never got any longer.
opinion sump for 1 : A neighbour can come to a doorway here with nothing and leave with a bit of supper in a folded rag.
opinion times against 2 : My cheapest meal still takes a whole morning of shoulder work to pay for.
opinion watch against 1 : I've seen too much time go into asking why a tired wolf has stopped to admire the stone he's standing on.

grown
line greet : There's a strip for standing beside my row.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : Mind that red chip. It's standing there on purpose.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. The frost's written on the stone again.
line greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Sit clear of the dug earth and take the last light.
line greet [self.working=yes] : I'm getting the weight down. Then you can have my ear.
line again.open : Back on this row with me.
line kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Family can take the broad garden stone.
line greet.return : Your call came clear across my little plot.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : Your voice is known here without any reckoning.
line farewell : Leave my red stone on the surface.
line farewell.return : I'll close this furrow up before dark.
line react.news : Which bit would stand up to being weighed?
line react.news.new : I'll need another mark to remember that.
line react.news.known : That entry's been made once already.
line react.news.doubt : Did the account come straight from someone on the load?
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : A pot can go quietly to a grieving household.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : Worth smoothing the soil over a good day's work.
line answer.how : Tired in an exact number of places.
line ask.how : Have you got your full day's due?
line sympathise : Some aches won't come off with the yard dirt.
line reassure : Set down what's heavy. I'll give it room.
line decline : I'd have to owe my own supper hour twice to take that on.
line accept_decline : Then that request can stay out of our reckoning.
line thank : A full measure of help. I'll remember.
line preclose : I've still one small hole to fill.
line ack : Paid fair.

scene pebble
when topic=land
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I put a white stone below the soil when I've settled what I owe.
b : Doesn't that cost a stone? | What if someone owes you?
a : Costs a bend at the waist. The stone stays in my possession. | I leave red brick showing. It's a reminder to ask once, plainly.

scene yard
when topic=work self.job=laborer self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A plank can look mighty short among a great pile and very long on the walk across the yard.
b : What's your test for weight? | Which supports should receive it?
a : Lift one end a thumb before taking the whole business. My back likes notice. | On sound supports. Bent planks take their rest out of somebody else's working day.

scene dig
when topic=pastimes self.likes=digging
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A narrow spade makes a small garden last.
b : Wouldn't you finish quicker with a wide one? | How deep are your rows?
a : Yes. Getting done quickly isn't all I enjoy about gardening. | Deep according to the root. I'm planting supper, not opening a gravel pit.

scene barley
when topic=food self.likes=barley_soup
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Well-cooked barley will split against my wooden spoon.
b : Is split grain good eating? | What if the pot's thin?
a : Good and soft. It sits warm inside after a long carry. | Give it a slow stir. Sometimes the thick bit's all below the surface.

scene map
when topic=lore self.likes=old_maps
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I own a map showing one ink road passing through another road's bridge.
b : What would happen at the crossing? | Could you correct it?
a : On paper, nothing. In a cart I'd stop and have a good look first. | Pencil would do it. I keep the old way visible to show what a sure hand can get wrong.

scene frost
when topic=weather self.likes=frosty_mornings
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The first frost picks out a spade mark more clearly than fresh rain.
b : Does that help the garden? | Would you dig then?
a : Helps the gardener see where the foot landed and packed the soil last night. | Later, once the point can go in without jarring my wrist.

scene crowd
when topic=smalltalk self.dislikes=crowds
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A crowd can take a great deal of space without bringing a decent patch of silence.
b : Would a wall help? | Do you go home from a fair?
a : At least I'd know one side couldn't lean against me. | Once I've bought the thing I came for. There's no prize for staying till my head aches.

scene price
when topic=prices self.dislikes=haggling
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like a charge I can remember after the first asking.
b : Would you try for a better price? | Suppose it's too dear to begin with?
a : I try a different seller, quite calmly. | Set the article back entire. Nobody can charge me extra for doing that.

scene sharesoup
when topic=family self.married=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd save a bit of warm soup to share at home with #self.spouse#.
b : Do you keep enough for two? | Why soup after a day of dirt?
a : Two bowls before I reckon what can go in the jar. | The dirt stays on my boots. Hot barley goes just where the work left a space.

scene sump
when topic=home self.quarter=sump
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A little patch of green doesn't show much from the Sump stairs unless a wolf stops to look.
b : What shows first? | Does the ground belong to you?
a : A new leaf with the edges still pinched together. I've got time to stop for that. | The plants have the use of it. I make no grander claim.

scene sail
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd take a berth that carried me far enough to hang up my coat in perfectly dry weather.
b : How far is enough? | Would you take your garden along?
a : I expect I'd know by the lighter feel across my shoulders. | A pinch of seed, maybe. Not much ballast required for such a notion.

scene weigh
when topic=work self.job=laborer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# I count my trips separate from the piles.
b : Why keep two counts? | Are all trips equal?
a : Several trips make one pile. I'd rather my pay had the full arithmetic. | No. Wet timber and dry timber don't take equal shares of a shoulder.

scene friend
when topic=smalltalk self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd be content to trade seeds with #self.friend# without putting either lot on the scales.
b : No entry in the account? | Why keep the agreement loose?
a : Presents aren't debts. An honest reckoning knows where to stop. | A plant that grows well is its own receipt.

scene rest
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : After carrying timber I put both palms on a flat stone a while.
b : Cold or warm? | Does it do much?
a : Either if the stone's smooth. I'm giving my fingers leave to stretch. | It brings my hands back to their ordinary size in my thoughts.

scene spring
when topic=season
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A wet row in early spring wants watching before anybody adds seed.
b : What's it waiting for? | How can waiting help?
a : A little air in the soil. Even barley needs more than wet earth closed about it. | I can mend my tools while the earth dries. No day entirely wasted.

scene ledger
when topic=prices self.wealth=poor|destitute
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I know where each copper in my pocket has agreed to go.
b : What about an unexpected expense? | Is there anything left for pleasure?
a : It means altering some other arrangement. That's why I notice the difference of a copper. | A garden's reasonable. It mostly asks the use of muscles already paid for.

scene dark
when topic=day here.time=dusk|night
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I lay the short spade flat when the light starts showing only its handle.
b : Why on its side? | How will you find it?
a : A tread on the blade otherwise lifts the handle smartly. I prefer getting up without the spade's assistance. | Along the same board every time. Habit's a cheap lantern.

story whitebrick [topic=land]
  : I buried a white pebble to mark a repaid copper and hit another pebble already there.
  : I'd chosen the same bare spot twice and come to rest on an old paid account.
  b : Did you move either stone?
  : I moved the new one a finger's width. Even settled debts deserve entries of their own.

story warmbarley [topic=food]
  : I kept a bowl warm by settling a smaller bowl across the rim.
  : A little cloud came up from under my improvised cover and cleared my nose more effectively than a sharp wind.
  b : Was the soup still hot?
  : Steaming. I gave the first spoonful the further courtesy of a little breath.

story wrongbridge [topic=travel]
  : I followed an old ink mark down to a lane that ended at a garden wall.
  : Above the wall I could see a turn of road just where my sheet claimed I should be standing.
  b : Did you jump across?
  : I added a little upright stroke for the wall and walked round carrying a better map.

rule @load
when concept=bark self.job=laborer self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Set the long end down on the bearer. | Keep both hands clear of the last inch.

rule @cold
when concept=bark self.likes=frosty_mornings
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Wait till the frost lets the spade in. | That's yesterday's heel in the white.

rule @soup
when concept=bark self.likes=barley_soup
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Stir up the grains along the bottom. | Two portions before the jar's share.

rule @dark
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Short iron flat on its side. | Leave a red chip showing for morning.
dlg resident.hub : My row's clear and my back could use a minute standing straight.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : You've seen my marker stones before, #topic.player#.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : Leave the reckoning on my side until I've heard yours.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=night] : The white stones show faintly from where you're standing.
dlg resident.job [self.job=laborer] : I carry what the yard needs shifted at #self.workplace#. I've learned to give each plank its length of room.
dlg resident.job : I'll take a sound day's load for a sum that doesn't change on the way to my pocket.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : Here's a little piece with the weight still on it. #world.news#.
dlg resident.bye : Stay on the firm slip beside the furrows.

graft @buriedcoin resident.hub
choice What grows from a buried pebble? -> buriedcoin
node buriedcoin
say Nothing edible. It marks a debt settled. The red chip I left above it tells me another little thing still needs attending to.
choice Why bury what you've finished paying? -> buriedcoin_more
choice Turn back from the row. -> hub
node buriedcoin_more
say Because I like going past without being reminded once the matter's properly done. The bit of ground looks better for the peace.
choice Turn back from the row. -> hub
choice Leave the stones settled. -> bye
